Complete Example

Suppose:

TCS Share

Support = ₹3500
Resistance = ₹3700

======


Intraday Trader (15 Min Chart)
Price falls to ₹3500
      ↓
Buy

Price rises to ₹3700
      ↓
Sell

=====


Investor (1 Month Chart)
Buy near ₹3500
Hold for several months
Sell above ₹3700 or higher
=======

Support is the price level where buyers stop the stock from falling further, 
while resistance is the price level where sellers stop the stock from rising further. 
Time frames represent the duration of each candlestick, such as 1 minute, 15 minutes, 1 day, 
or 1 month, and are used by different types of traders to analyze market trends.
